# __FIA_DISPLAY_NAME__

This project was created with FIA Framework 0.5.

```bash
bun run dev
bun run build
bun run run
```

`bun run dev` launches the Swift Host with React HMR. Changes under `mcp.app.watch` restart only the
application MCP server. `bun run build` creates a signed macOS app containing a static UI and
standalone MCP server binaries; the resulting application does not require Bun to be installed.

The UI uses `@semicoder/fia/mcp` for application extensions and `@semicoder/fia/native` for typed
desktop APIs. Both use MCP `2026-07-28` through the Host's WebKit transport.

## Preset UI library

The editable component library lives in `src/ui/components/ui` and is exported from its `index.ts`.
Import components from the local barrel:

```tsx
import { Button, Dialog, Field, Input, useToast } from "./components/ui";
```

It includes primitives, form controls, navigation, overlays, notifications, and a light/dark/system
theme. `src/ui/main.tsx` already installs `ThemeProvider` and `ToastProvider`, while
`src/ui/style.css` imports the component design tokens and styles. Keep those providers mounted when
using `useTheme` or `useToast`; edit the local components and CSS directly to adapt the design.

## MCP boundary

`src/mcp/server.ts` exports a synchronous `defineMcpServer` factory. FIA generates the stdio entry and
rejects legacy MCP clients. Keep structured control data under 1 MiB on MCP; use explicit file paths
or another purpose-built channel for large media.

Additional servers may be configured in `mcp.servers`. They must be executable arm64 Mach-O files
inside the project and are copied, verified, and signed into the application.
